Z||000032||88CoupeV6||07-09-2001||03:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>Thanks, I just washed it.  The car was repainted in May but no wax yet.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You do have a super sweet Fiero. I love it. I can't tell you how much I want it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I haven't waxed my 88 coupe either. I got it painted in April. I just use P21s pure polish. It has no sealers or waxes in it. Just natural oils the paint needs and it can still breath for curing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000033||skitime||07-09-2001||03:40 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88CoupeV6:<BR><B> You do have a super sweet Fiero. I love it. I can't tell you how much I want it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I haven't waxed my 88 coupe either. I got it painted in April. I just use P21s pure polish. It has no sealers or waxes in it. Just natural oils the paint needs and it can still breath for curing.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the compliment.  The car was painted with all panels removed so that everything is perfect. I really haven't waxed it yet because I want to do some more mods that will require repainting some panels. I posted more picture of the car on the thread "Hey Skitime" <P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
